; ── R modulo ASSOCIATIVITY: the actual theory (Church–Rosser MODULO A) ──
; cmp is ASSOCIATIVE but NOT commutative ⇒ this is modulo-A, not modulo-AC.
; The associativity is a CONGRUENCE (theory), the elimination rules are oriented
; ON TOP of it.  The critical pair above becomes JOINABLE MODULO A (its two reducts
; are one assoc-step apart).  Claim: R is confluent + terminating MODULO A ⇒ unique
; normal forms modulo A ⇒ decidable equality.  This is "have both A and B".
;
; NOTE on syntax: pure modulo-A is less standardised than AC.  If your tool wants the
; theory inline, the intended declaration is the associativity equation as E:
(VAR x y z)
(THEORY
  (EQUATIONS
    cmp(cmp(x,y),z) == cmp(x,cmp(y,z))
  )
)
(RULES
  cmp(x,od(y))     -> od(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(os(x),os(y)) -> os(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(od(x),os(y)) -> od(cmp(x,y))
  cmp(oz,oz)       -> oz
)
